WEBVTT

00:00:00.366 --> 00:00:09.731
Food safety keeps your temperature and hygiene checks on schedule, and on the record. In this video, you’ll log a check, deal with a problem, and print the report.

00:00:10.754 --> 00:00:20.546
Open Food safety. Today shows every check due at this location: coolers, freezer, hot holding, sanitizer and more, with what’s due, late, or missed.

00:00:21.565 --> 00:00:28.861
Click Log reading, and type what the thermometer says. Here, the walk-in is at 45 degrees, which is out of range.

00:00:29.879 --> 00:00:39.010
So Worklynq asks what was done about it, and opens a Food Safety Issue ticket for the manager. You can also just tell Assist, walk-in is 38.

00:00:40.035 --> 00:00:46.755
Report is the week-by-week log an inspector asks for, with every problem and what was done about it, ready to print.

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:53.711
In Set up, choose the checks, their limits in Fahrenheit or Celsius, and how often each one is due.
